# Project Tasks: HR Minds (Agentic RAG)

- [x] 1. Project Setup
  - Description: Initialize environment variables, database connections, and infrastructure for local development and documentation.
  - Subtasks:
    - [x] Create and configure `.env` and `.env.example` files with required secrets and environment variables
    - [x] Configure `config.py` with Pydantic settings and `.env` loading via `python-dotenv`
    - [x] Configure `docker-compose.yml` for PostgreSQL (credentials & port read from `.env`)
    - [x] Document setup instructions, run commands, and architecture in `README.md`

- [x] 2. ORM & Database Migration Setup
  - Description: Configure SQLAlchemy async engine, base models, mixins, and Alembic migrations.
  - Subtasks:
    - [x] Set up async database connection, session factory (`AsyncSessionLocal`), and `get_db` dependency (`settings/db.py`)
    - [x] Add `TimestampMixin` (id, created, modified) and auto-generated snake_case table naming convention in `Base`
    - [x] Initialize Alembic with async template at `src/hr_minds/migrations`
    - [x] Configure Alembic `env.py` for model auto-discovery and dynamic database URL resolution
    - [x] Create initial User model (`auth/models.py`) and document migration workflow in `migrations/README`

- [x] 3. Auth
  - Description: Implement secure user authentication mechanisms.
  - Subtasks:
    - [x] Implement user registration & secure password hashing (Argon2 via pwdlib)
    - [x] Implement login endpoint returning JWT access/refresh tokens (`POST /api/v1/auth/token`)
    - [x] Implement logout endpoint (session revocation via `AccessToken` table)
    - [x] Implement dependency for current authenticated user (`get_current_user`) and RBAC `require()`

- [ ] 4. Media Upload (Local Storage)
  - Description: Implement file storage handling for resumes and documents using local disk storage (omitting AWS S3 for now).
  - Subtasks:
    - [ ] Create media upload router and validation schemas (PDF/Docx validation)
    - [ ] Configure local storage adapter (saving files to a local `uploads/` directory)
    - [ ] Implement endpoint to upload resume files and store file metadata in PostgreSQL DB
    - [ ] Implement file retrieval / download endpoint

- [ ] 5. Recruitment Module (Agentic RAG Resume Filtering)
  - Description: Implement recruitment pipelines where uploaded resumes from the media module are automatically processed, parsed, and filtered against HR job descriptions using Agentic RAG.
  - Subtasks:
    - [ ] Create Job Description (JD) management model and endpoints (create/list JDs)
    - [ ] Implement resume text parsing service (PDF/Docx text extraction)
    - [ ] Implement text chunking, embedding generation, and vector retrieval pipeline
    - [ ] Build Agentic RAG evaluation/filtering engine to match candidates against JDs and score resume relevance
    - [ ] Create recruitment matching endpoints to query candidates and view AI evaluation summaries
